{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3275","artifact_type":"code-review","name":"plan/code-review-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md@sha256:c1434c5130c3cc2a61a70a7e43712d8f31a21e3b3d5864d7c9ba760f0ef6dbce"},"owner_reference":"3275","content":"# Code Review: Provider-Neutral Cache-Bypass (backlog #3275)\n\n**Verdict: PASS**\n\nScope reviewed: commits `53f0e43d2` (T1 rename), `488d5c542` + `6520637b6` (T3 view_item refresh,\ncorrected), `3efc4d7df` (T2 test renames), `00d7b7c27` (doc fix), `bc360962c` + `422e191ff` (T4/T5\ntest coverage), `0f8ef1217` (T6 docs), against feature plan P4cab86c1 (tasks T1-T6) and the\narchitect spec (`artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\"architect\")`, corrected post-T3).\n\n## Verification performed\n\n- Full pytest run across all touched suites: `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`,\n  `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`, `tests/test_scenarios.py`,\n  `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py`, `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py`,\n  `backlog_core/tests/**` \u2014 **1049 passed, 0 failed**.\n- `ruff check` on all 8 modified production/test files \u2014 clean.\n- `ty check` on the 3 modified production files (`operations.py`, `server.py`,\n  `sam_schema/backlog.py`) \u2014 clean.\n- Re-ran the exact acceptance-criteria commands from T1 and T3 (signature assertions for\n  `list_items`/`view_item`, the `from_github` scope grep) \u2014 all pass as specified.\n- `git diff --stat` across the full commit range: exactly the 10 expected files plus 3\n  `plugin.json` version bumps (unrelated, auto-managed) \u2014 no generated docs\n  (`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `graphify-out/graph.json`) touched, per constraint.\n\n## Findings by task\n\n**T1 (rename `from_github`\u2192`refresh` on `backlog_list`/`list_items`)** \u2014 Clean, positional slot\npreserved, no deprecation shim (per ADR-2), provider-neutral wording. Matches spec \u00a74.1/4.2\nverbatim.\n\n**T2 (test rename)** \u2014 Mechanical, all 10+ call sites updated, no assertions weakened,\n`test_live_validation.py:286` correctly left untouched (confirmed false positive).\n\n**T3 (`refresh` on `view_item`/`backlog_view`/CLI `view`)** \u2014 This is the highest-risk task and\nthe one place a real defect surfaced mid-implementation: the original ADR-3 (gate the\nalready-unconditional numeric-selector live check behind `refresh`) contradicted 52 pre-existing\ntests in `backlog_core/tests/` that assert that behavior stays unconditional. This was caught\nduring T3's own CoVe check (not by this review), escalated, and corrected in `6520637b6`\n(`if refresh:` \u2192 `if issue_num or refresh:`) plus `00d7b7c27` (Field description rewrite). Verified\nthe corrected code against the full A-H truth table in the corrected spec \u2014 all 8 rows check out\nagainst the current `operations.py:2947-2964`. `_live_lookup_id()` never returns `\"\"`, never\nforwards a raw title into `view_enrich_from_github()`, and `result.groomed` is preserved on every\npath where `item` exists.\n\n**Minor finding (non-blocking):** `view_item()`'s own docstring `Args:` block for `refresh`\n(`operations.py:2922-2928`) was not updated when `6520637b6`/`00d7b7c27` corrected the behavior.\nIt still reads \"a selector that already resolves to a local item returns the cached copy without a\nnetwork call\" \u2014 this is now false for numeric/#N/URL selectors, which always live-check\nregardless of `refresh` (only title-substring selectors are gated). `server.py`'s MCP `Field`\ndescription was correctly updated in the same pass; the `operations.py` docstring was missed. No\ntest or acceptance criterion asserts docstring content, so this doesn't block PASS, but it's a\nreal doc/code mismatch that will mislead a future reader of `operations.py` in isolation from\n`server.py`. Recommend a one-line follow-up fix (mirror the corrected `server.py` wording into the\n`Args:` block).\n\n**T4/T5 (test coverage)** \u2014 Regression guards mutation-checked with red/green evidence in the\ntask handoff (verified independently: I did not re-run the mutation myself, but the described\nmutations and failure messages are consistent with the actual code paths). Scenario coverage\nmatches the corrected spec's 6-scenario list, with scenario 5 (beads nanoid) correctly identified\nas pre-existing coverage rather than duplicated. CLI file gained its first `list`/`view` coverage\n(previously zero, confirmed by grep). Patch targets (`sam_schema.backlog.operations.*`,\n`backlog_core.operations.*`) match each file's existing convention.\n\n**T6 (docs)** \u2014 `SKILL.md`/`README.md` wording verified against the actual shipped `Field`\ndescriptions in `server.py` (not the spec draft) \u2014 matches verbatim for both `backlog_list` and\n`backlog_view`. Generated artifacts correctly left untouched with a handoff note that they need\n`dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh`.\n\n## Scope/quality checks\n\n- No deprecation aliases or backward-compat shims for `from_github` anywhere in the diff (ADR-2).\n- No new reconciliation logic \u2014 `view_enrich_from_github()` reused as-is on every path (ADR-5).\n- No new field on `ViewItemResult`/`ViewItemResultCompact`; `models.py` untouched.\n- `backlog_list_followups`/CLI `list-followups` untouched (ADR-4, correctly out of scope).\n- No plain `bool` replaced with an enum/Literal (spec \u00a76 constraint honored).\n\n## Recommendation\n\nPASS. One non-blocking documentation follow-up identified above (stale `Args:` docstring text in\n`operations.py:2922-2928`); does not require a new task, small enough to fix in TN-verification or\nas a fast-follow.\n"}